From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: arm64: dts: h713: hy300-2023: the fw202312 unit's AFBD handoff words

The second unit of the board hy300-2023 (issue #11, variant fw202312)
runs the "ADT-3 2024-09" display.bin (49f698af...), not the 2023-06
unit's. 0350 said that the handoff words of a display firmware nobody
has run would show up as a refusal of the AFBD driver, and that is what
its owner's serial console showed on 18.11.2026, in two boots of the
TEST image hy300-2023-fw202312-test1:

  sun50i-h713-afbd 5600000.display: error -ENODEV: video handoff state
  is not this board's: CTRL 03001901 (expected 03001901), VIDEO_CTRL
  03000200 (expected 03000010), selector 00000000 (expected 29000000)
  -- the node has no allwinner,handoff-state

The three words found are the ones the HY320 measured for "ADT-3 2024"
(0335) and the HY300 T08's tree carries (0349). The handoff words belong
to the firmware, not to the board, and the two units of this board run
two firmwares, so the fw202312 unit gets a tree of its own: the
hy300-2023 tree with these three words. The 2023-06 unit's tree stays
as it is; its firmware's words are still not known.

The owner has opened the unit since: the silkscreen is
HY300_T08_QZ713_V3, the HY300 T08's. Nothing else is taken from the T08
tree here: the T08's elog addresses are those of another display.bin,
and this tree keeps the focus motor off as the hy300-2023 tree does.

Not known: whether a picture follows. The same two logs show U-Boot
reporting its boot logo up while the wall stayed black, which the AFBD
refusal does not explain. The elog addresses stay the HY300 Pro's.

Built (dtc, against the series applied to 6.18.38); not booted.

diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
@@ -64,6 +64,7 @@ dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-l018.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy320.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy300-t08.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy300-2023.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy300-2023-fw202312.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-h728-x96qpro+.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-t527-avaota-a1.dtb
diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-2023-fw202312.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-2023-fw202312.dts
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-2023-fw202312.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+/*
+ * MagCubic HY300 with the 2023-12 ADT-3 firmware (issue #11): the second
+ * unit of the board hy300-2023, variant fw202312. Silkscreen
+ * HY300_T08_QZ713_V3 (its owner, 18.11.2026). Its display firmware is the
+ * "ADT-3 2024-09" display.bin, not the 2023-06 unit's.
+ *
+ * The hy300-2023 tree, plus the one thing that belongs to that firmware and
+ * was read off this unit: the AFBD handoff words. With the HY300 Pro's
+ * defaults the driver refused in both boots of the first TEST image (the
+ * owner's serial log, 18.11.2026), and the words it found are the ones
+ * below - the same three the HY320 measured for "ADT-3 2024" (0335).
+ *
+ * Not this unit's: the elog addresses, which stay the HY300 Pro's. Not
+ * known: whether a picture follows; U-Boot's boot logo was not visible on
+ * this unit either. The image built from this is a TEST image for its owner.
+ */
+
+#include "sun50i-h713-hy300-2023.dts"
+
+/ {
+	model = "MagCubic HY300 (2023 firmware, fw202312)";
+	compatible = "magcubic,hy300-2023-fw202312", "magcubic,hy300-2023",
+		     "allwinner,sun50i-h713";
+};
+
+/*
+ * What the "ADT-3 2024-09" firmware leaves in the AFBD: CTRL, VIDEO_CTRL,
+ * selector (read off this unit, 18.11.2026).
+ */
+&display {
+	allwinner,handoff-state = <0x03001901 0x03000200 0x00000000>;
+};
